<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26493" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lĭbīdĭnor</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lŭbīd-</span></b> ), āri,
			v. dep.
		id, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to
				indulge</i> or <i>gratify lust</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum libidinatur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. 7, 67, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inceste libidinari,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Ner. 28 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">abeunt libidinatum ad filias Moab,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. ad Gnost. 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Petr. 138, 7</span></i>.</div>
